NAME
       vgs - list LVM volume groups in a short table

SYNOPSIS
       vgs [-a] [-o FIELDS] [-O SORT] [-S SELECTION] [--noheadings]
           [--units UNIT] [--nosuffix] [--separator TEXT] [VG...]

DESCRIPTION
       vgs prints one line per volume group:

       VG     the name.
       #PV    how many physical volumes it is made of.
       #LV    how many logical volumes it holds.
       #SN    how many snapshots.
       Attr   attributes; the first letter w means writable, the third
              letter n the normal allocation policy.
       VSize  the total size.
       VFree  the space not yet given to any LV.

       Sizes are shown in convenient units with a letter (m for MiB, g for
       GiB) and a < in front when the value was rounded.

       With -o you choose the columns, which together with --noheadings
       makes vgs good for scripts and checks.

OPTIONS
       -o, --options FIELDS
              The columns to show, comma separated. Useful fields: vg_name,
              pv_count, lv_count, vg_size, vg_free, vg_extent_size,
              vg_extent_count, vg_free_count, vg_uuid. -o +FIELD adds a
              column to the default ones.

       --noheadings
              Leave out the header line.

       --units UNIT
              Show sizes in this unit: b, k, m, g, t (powers of 1024), or
              upper case for powers of 1000.

       --nosuffix
              Leave the unit letter off the sizes (with --units).

       --separator TEXT
              Separate columns with TEXT instead of spaces.

       -O, --sort FIELDS
              Sort by these fields (a - in front sorts in reverse).

       -S, --select SELECTION
              Only volume groups that match, such as -S 'vg_free > 0'.

       -a, --all
              Include everything LVM knows about.

EXAMPLES
       List all volume groups:

           vgs

       Print the extent size of vgdata, for a test:

           vgs --noheadings -o vg_extent_size vgdata

       Show the free space in MiB, without the unit letter:

           vgs --noheadings --units m --nosuffix -o vg_free vgdata

SEE ALSO
       pvs(8), lvs(8), vgdisplay(8), vgcreate(8), vgextend(8)
